# London Bridge Is Falling Down — traditional English (public domain), in G.
# Arranged by the Piano Practice contributors (MIT): the hands take turns in middle-C
# position. Right hand C D E (fingers 1 2 3), left hand G A B (fingers 4 3 2).
# The tune never uses F, so it is written without a key signature.
title: London Bridge
composer: Traditional
arranger: Piano Practice contributors
time: 4/4
key: 0
tempo: 96
license: Public domain (traditional), arrangement MIT
---
RH: d4/4 e4 d4 c4 | r/4 c4 d4/2 | r/2 c4/2    | r/4 c4 d4/2 |
LH: r/1           | b3/4 r/2.   | a3/4 b3 r/2 | b3/4 r/2.   |

RH: d4/4 e4 d4 c4 | r/4 c4 d4/2 | r/2 d4/2 | r/1       |
LH: r/1           | b3/4 r/2.   | a3/2 r/2 | b3/2 g3/2 |
